          "kind": "informational",
          "level": "none",
          "guid": "mt36yljw8qtxqwd8",
          "message": {
            "text": "Stacking and fixed ownership intentionally use different Blink predicates. At Chromium 7d859f27, ComputedStyle records active perspective as a stacking reason, LayoutInline::LayerTypeRequired decides whether that style reason has a paint layer, and LayoutObject::ComputeIsFixedContainer separately adds an IsBox gate. The captured fact therefore rejects static non-box inlines for both paint/fixed activation, while relative positioning preserves the inline stacking boundary without manufacturing fixed ownership. Computed preserve-3d remains fixed-owning through grouping-property flattening.",
            "markdown": "Stacking and fixed ownership intentionally use different Blink predicates. At Chromium 7d859f27, ComputedStyle records active perspective as a stacking reason, LayoutInline::LayerTypeRequired decides whether that style reason has a paint layer, and LayoutObject::ComputeIsFixedContainer separately adds an IsBox gate. The captured fact therefore rejects static non-box inlines for both paint/fixed activation, while relative positioning preserves the inline stacking boundary without manufacturing fixed ownership. Computed preserve-3d remains fixed-owning through grouping-property flattening."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/render/stacking.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 9,
                  "endLine": 37,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "/**\n * Live captures set this false when Blink declines to make this layout object\n * a fixed-position containing block for its transform-related computed state\n * (notably a normal `display:inline` span). This is deliberately narrower than\n * stacking-context creation: ComputedStyle can still classify a positioned\n * inline as a stacking context even though LayoutObject::IsBox() rejects it as\n * a fixed container. Older/synthetic trees omit the fact and retain the\n * computed-style fallback.\n */\nfunction transformRelatedCanOwnFixed(el: CapturedElement): boolean {\n  return el.styles.transformRelatedBox !== false;\n}\n\n/**\n * A box gets a PaintLayer for its computed transform-related stacking reason.\n * A non-box LayoutInline does not, unless relative positioning independently\n * makes LayoutInline::LayerTypeRequired return a layer. Other inline layer\n * reasons (grouping, animation, containment, sticky) are already independent\n * SC checks below.\n */\nfunction transformRelatedCreatesStackingBoundary(el: CapturedElement): boolean {\n  return transformRelatedCanOwnFixed(el)\n    || (el.styles.display === \"inline\" && el.styles.position === \"relative\");\n}\n\nconst transformRelatedWillChangeProperties: ReadonlySet<string> = new Set([\n  \"transform\", \"transform-style\", \"perspective\", \"translate\", \"rotate\",\n  \"scale\", \"offset-path\", \"offset-position\",\n]);"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
